          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            %em Steenrod squares
            is the system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+operations"} cohomology operations
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"} cyclic group of order 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            (the “stable cohomology operations”). They are special examples of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+operations"} power operations
          %p
            The collection of Steenrod squares for all degrees forms the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steenrod+algebra"} Steenrod algebra
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#DefinitionInTermsOfExtendedSquares Construction in terms of extended squares
          %p
            We discuss the explicit construction of the Steenrod-operations in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+maps"} chain maps
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            equipped with a suitable product. We follow (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie07"}> Lurie 07, lecture 2
            ).
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2 \coloneqq \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            with two elements.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V^{\otimes n}_{h \Sigma_n} \in \mathbb{F}_2 Mod
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            of the
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            with itself by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            by the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinvariants"} coinvariants
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_n(V)
            of the tensor product of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{\otimes n}
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+resolution"} free resolution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \Sigma_n^\bullet
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V^{\otimes n}_{h \Sigma_n}
                  \\simeq
                  D_n(V)
                  \\coloneqq
                  (V^{\otimes n} \otimes E\Sigma_n)_{\Sigma_n}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is called the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+power"} extended power
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p For instance
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D_2(  \mathbb{F}_2[-n])
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathbb{F}_2[-2n] \otimes C^\bullet(B \Sigma_2)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right we have the, say,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast //\Sigma_2 \simeq B \Sigma_2 \simeq \mathbb{R}P^\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_2
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D_2(V) \longrightarrow V
          %p
            is called a
            %em symmetric multiplication
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            (a shadow of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+algebra"} E-infinity algebra
            structure). The archetypical class of examples of these are given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = C^\bullet(X, \mathbb{F}_2)
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \Sigma_2
          %p
            Therefore there is a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^k(D_2(\mathbb{F}_2[-n]))
                  \\simeq
                  H_{2n - k}(B \Sigma_2, \mathbb{F}_2) e_{2n}
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
            of the extended square of the chain compplex concentrated on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
            in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            of this classifying space shifted by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 n
          %p
            Using this one gets for general
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \leq n
            a map that sends an element in the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [v] \in H^n(V)
          %p
            represented by a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  v \;\colon\; \mathbb{F}_2[-n] \longrightarrow V
          %p to the element
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi Sq
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overline{Sq}^i(v) \in H^{n+1}(D_2(V))
          %p
            represented by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{F}_2[-n-i]
                  \\stackrel{1}{\longrightarrow}
                  C^\bullet(B \Sigma_2, \mathbb{F}_2)
                  \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  D_2(\mathbb{F}_2[-n])
                  \\stackrel{D_2(v)}{\longrightarrow}
                  D_2(V)
                  \\,.
          %p
            If moreover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is equipped with a
            %em symmetric product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_2(V) \longrightarrow V
            as above, then one can further compose and form the element
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Sq
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {Sq}^i(v) \in H^{n+1}(V)
          %p
            represented by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi V
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{F}_2[-n-i]
                  \\stackrel{1}{\longrightarrow}
                  C^\bullet(B \Sigma_2, \mathbb{F}_2)
                  \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  D_2(\mathbb{F}_2[-n])
                  \\stackrel{D_2(v)}{\longrightarrow}
                  D_2(V)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  V
                  \\,.
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Sq
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sq^i \;\colon\; H^\bullet(V) \longrightarrow H^{\bullet + i}(V)
          %p
            is called the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %em Steenrod operation
            or the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %em Steenrod square
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = C^\bullet(X,\mathbb{F}_2)
            the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular cochain complex
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Sq
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sq^i \;\colon\; H^\bullet(X, \mathbb{F}_2) \longrightarrow H^{\bullet+i}(X,\mathbb{F}_2)
                  \\,.
          %h3#axiomatic_characterization Axiomatic characterization
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^n \mathbb{Z}_2
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+order+2"} group of order 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{Z}_2,n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} of topological spaces
          %p
            Notice that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            any topological space (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"}> CW-complex
            ),
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n(X, \mathbb{Z}_2) \coloneqq H(X, B^n \mathbb{Z}_2)
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^{k}(-, \mathbb{Z}_2) \to H^l(-, \mathbb{Z}_2)
          %p
            correspond bijectively to morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi l
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^k \mathbb{Z}_2 \to B^l \mathbb{Z}_2
          %p
            The following characterization is due to (
            %a{:href => "#SteenrodEpstein"}> SteenrodEpstein
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong Steenrod squares
              are a collection of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+operations"} cohomology operations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sq^n \;\colon\; H^k(-, \mathbb{Z}_2) \longrightarrow H^{k+n}(-, \mathbb{Z}_2)
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Sq
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sq^n \;\colon\; B^k \mathbb{Z}_2 \longrightarrow B^{k + n} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %p
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n,k \in \mathbb{N}
              satisfying the following conditions:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
                  it is the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt deg(x)
                  then
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Sq
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sq^n(x) = 0
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = n
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Sq
                          %mi n
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sq^n : B^n \mathbb{Z}_2 \to B^{2n} \mathbb{Z}_2
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∪
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto x \cup x
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Sq
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo +
                            %mi j
                            %mo =
                            %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi Sq
                          %mi i
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi Sq
                          %mi j
                        %mi y
